WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.350
Thor: Ragnarok is a huge hit with critics
and audiences and sends its titular hero off

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.300
on a bold new adventure that boasts long-time
ramifications for him, his friends, and for

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:11.780
Asgard.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.580
It also sets up a new three-film trilogy arc
for the Hulk, who plays a major role alongside

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.090
our title hero.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.140
Naturally, it leaves some plot threads dangling,
with lingering questions that range from Loki's

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.789
allegiance to how Ragnarok will affect the
upcoming Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:31.770
Many of these stories will be picked up in
future Marvel films, but some are a bit more

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.500
nebulous and may not be answered for quite
some time—if ever.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.760
Let's take a look at some of the biggest questions
left unanswered by Thor: Ragnarok.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.110
It should go without saying, but brace for
spoilers ahead!

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.880
Is Hulk here to stay?

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.900
We find out in Ragnarok's second act that
Bruce Banner has been in his Hulk form for

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.760
two whole years, and he later describes this
particular transformation as different from

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.770
any other.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.550
Apparently, his consciousness has been absent
all the while, with only Hulk and no Banner

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.220
knocking around in his mind.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.540
"Hulk like fire."

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.830
He's afraid that if he transforms again, he
may never be able to revert back to Banner.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.490
But that doesn't stop him from transforming
into Hulk again when when Thor's ragtag Revengers

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.740
find themselves in desperate need against
Hela's forces and the giant demon Surtur.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.270
Now we're left to wonder whether we'll see
Bruce Banner as we know him again.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.600
Where's Sif?

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.050
Sif really dodged a bullet in Thor: Ragnarok's
first act by not being available to charge

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.930
against Hela with her cohorts.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.500
That being said, we've gotta wonder where
she's at during this movie.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:38.450
Sif gets nary a mention throughout the entirety
of Ragnarok, which is strange considering

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.250
her prominence in the prior two films in the
series.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:41.750
"WHAT."

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:47.340
Admittedly we know her absence is due to actress
Jaimie Alexander filming her TV show Blindspot,

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.940
but that doesn't quite explain the decision
not to mention her at all.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.659
You'd think a throwaway line explaining she
was off-world might have been warranted, considering

00:01:55.659 --> 00:02:00.940
she had a couple significant appearances in
Marvel's Agents of Shield television series.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.690
Has Loki turned good for good?

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:06.000
Has the God of Mischief permanently turned
over a new leaf?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.420
That might depend on whether he took the Tesseract,
and leaked footage from D23 seems to indicate

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.420
that he did.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.470
But at the end of Ragnarok, we see him at
a tepid peace with his brother and the people

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.470
of Asgard.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:22.530
He fights valiantly in the battle of Ragnarok
and shares a quiet, friendly moment with Thor

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.350
in its aftermath, seeming to confirm that
he wants their relationship to heal.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:31.200
He even seems to support Thor taking his rightful
place on the throne as king of Asgard.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.030
But as Marvel fans know all too well, nothing
with Loki is as it seems.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.410
Even if his aiding Thor's cause in Ragnarok
comes from a sincere place, there's a very

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:44.230
good chance that it also serves as a stepping
stone on Loki's path to retaking the throne

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.819
and doing away with his brother.

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:47.819
Where will New Asgard be?

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:53.150
As Thor: Ragnarok comes to an end, the realm
of Asgard is destroyed by Surtur.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:58.230
Asgard was the first true foray into the cosmic
side of the Marvel universe and has served

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:03.239
a crucial role in the movies' world-building
over the last few years—and just like that,

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:04.260
it's gone.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.840
Fortunately, Thor and the Revengers successfully
evacuate the realm's citizens, so the casualty

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.700
count is low, but the film still ends with
an entire population adrift in space.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.700
Something similar happened in the comics that
landed Thor and all of Asgard in the middle

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.700
of Oklahoma.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.810
So, who knows?

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.220
Maybe this is just an easy way to let Thor
rule his kingdom a little closer to the Avengers

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.770
action for Infinity War?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.800
We just know that all of those Asgardians
have to go somewhere, and their newly-crowned

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.069
King Thor needs a kingdom.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:33.450
Whose ship is that?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:38.200
In the first of two post-credits sequences,
the Asgardian refugee ship is shown being

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.190
confronted by a massive spaceship of unknown
origin.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:46.770
We're never shown who's piloting it, but Marvel's
Kevin Feige has dubbed the vessel the Sanctuary

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:51.440
II, which means it's most likely the flagship
of Thanos, who's edging ever nearer to our

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.080
heroes as the impending Infinity War is getting
closer.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.520
Is Surtur dead?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.640
Surtur, a hellish monster prophesied to bring
about the titular end of days, makes his debut

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.190
in Thor: Ragnarok—and, sure enough, he does
just that.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:10.170
The film ends with his ultimate destruction
of Asgard, and with it, his apparent death.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.940
We can only assume he perished along with
the realm—along with Hela, the Goddess of

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.359
Death, but we don't actually see anyone die.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:18.539
We only see them disappear.

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:23.340
As Ragnarok is an event that functions cyclically,
having happened before and almost definitely

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.289
happening again someday, who can say for sure
that Surtur is dead?

00:04:27.289 --> 00:04:31.139
Perhaps he's simply gone back to his realm
to start the cycle over again.

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:33.800
Will Thor get Mjolnir back?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.749
One of the more shocking moments in Thor:
Ragnarok comes in its first act, when Hela

00:04:37.749 --> 00:04:40.789
crushes Thor's hammer, Mjolnir, with her bare
hand.

00:04:40.789 --> 00:04:46.050
It's a huge moment, as Mjolnir is thought
to be indestructible; perhaps even more surprising

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.819
is the fact that he doesn't get Mjolnir back
by the time the film is over.

00:04:49.819 --> 00:04:53.870
Admittedly, part of the character's arc is
coming into his own as the rightful king of

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:58.060
Asgard and the God of Thunder—, Mjolnir
only helps him channel his powers.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.060
It isn't their source.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:03.560
Still, a Thor without a hammer seems somewhat
naked, and we can't help but wonder if he'll

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.889
be getting his favorite toy back.

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:08.330
"Every time I threw it it would always come
back to me."

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:12.050
Mjolnir looked pretty busted after Hela had
her way with it, but when dealing with Norse

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:16.789
mythology and comic book characters, practicality
isn't really a priority.

00:05:16.789 --> 00:05:20.610
Don't be surprised if these two find a way
back together.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.659
Thanks for watching!

00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:24.469
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:24.469 --> 00:05:26.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

